dma-buf: sync_file: log unknown requests (diagnostic)

JetPack 4's user space was built for Android's older sync requests on fence
fds; 5.10's sync_file refuses them with ENOTTY, silently. Log each refused
request, rate limited, as "sync_file: unknown ioctl 0x... from <task>".

A diagnostic, kept in the build because 0026's second hunk has these lines
as context. With 0026 applied, the requests JetPack 4's video converter
makes are served, and trial 36 logged none.

Used in: trial 35, where it named the two requests 0026 then added.

Licence: GPL-2.0-only. Lab notes, with every measurement: NOTES.md.
---
diff --git a/drivers/dma-buf/sync_file.c b/drivers/dma-buf/sync_file.c
index f0c822952..bd8ac62be 100644
--- a/drivers/dma-buf/sync_file.c
+++ b/drivers/dma-buf/sync_file.c
@@ -473,6 +473,13 @@ static long sync_file_ioctl(struct file *file, unsigned int cmd,
 		return sync_file_ioctl_fence_info(sync_file, arg);
 
 	default:
+		/*
+		 * Jetson Nano trial: JetPack 4's userspace was built for
+		 * Android's older sync interface (ioctls 0 to 2 on the same
+		 * '>' type); show any request this one lacks.
+		 */
+		pr_warn_ratelimited("sync_file: unknown ioctl 0x%x from %s\n",
+				    cmd, current->comm);
 		return -ENOTTY;
 	}
 }
